<title>LUXEMBOURG: Ministers approve 1997 fish tariff quotas.</title>
<headline>Ministers approve 1997 fish tariff quotas.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fisheries ministers agreed on Monday by a qualified majority vote on autonomous import tariff quotas for 1997, EU officials said.</p>
<p>The quotas, which were opposed by France, Spain and Ireland, are intended to guarantee supplies at competitive prices for fish processors while protecting the interests of EU fishermen.</p>
<p>The quotas were as follows:</p>
<p> Product				Quantity     Duty    Period</p>
<p>					     (tonnes)  (percent)</p>
<p> Fresh, chilled or frozen cod   50,000	 4.0     Apr/Dec</p>
<p> Frozen cod			   15,000	 4.0     Apr/Dec</p>
<p> Cod livers				400	 0.0     Apr/Dec</p>
<p> Salted cod			    9,000	 4.0     Apr/Dec</p>
<p>Fresh, chilled or frozen</p>
<p> shrimps and prawns		  6,000	 0.0     1/3/97</p>
<p>								    to 31/3/98</p>
<p> Frozen surimi			 4,500	 6.0     Apr/Dec</p>
<p> Blue grenadier fillets	    4,000	 6.0     Apr/Dec</p>
<p> Tubes of Squid			7,000	 4.0     Apr/Dec</p>
<p> Frozen squid			    500	 4.0     Apr/Dec</p>
<p> Herring				23,000	 0.0     15/9/97</p>
<p>								    to 14/2/98</p>
<p> Tuna loin fillets and skipjack  1,000	12.0     Apr/Dec</p>
<p>EU officials said that France opposed the tuna loin and Ireland the herring measures, officials said.</p>
</text>
